//@ run-pass
//@ expect-stdout: 1 chain3

// Three levels, and only the LEAF declares the effect. This is the witness that discriminates
// local widening from real propagation — a distinction the error count cannot make, because both
// designs drive E035 to 0.
//
// Run it as:
//   SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER=1 SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER_TRACE=1 <madaros> --check <this file>
// and the trace must show TWO lines:
//   effect_infer: mid += Mut (from leaf)
//   effect_infer: top += Mut (from mid)
// The second line only exists if `mid` PUBLISHED the inferred effect into its own signature. With
// widening alone, `top` would compare against mid's empty declared set and learn nothing.
//
// Default behaviour (no SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER) is unchanged: this file reports E035, because `mid`
// and `top` mutate through an exclusive reference without declaring Mut. That is the shipped
// semantics and this test does not alter it — it is a run-pass because the PROGRAM is correct;
// what varies is whether the checker demands the annotation or infers it.

struct S {
    v: i64,
}

fn leaf(s: &!S) with Mut {
    (*s).v = 1
}

fn mid(s: &!S) {
    leaf(s)
}

fn top(s: &!S) {
    mid(s)
}

fn main() with IO, Mut, Panic, Div {
    var x = S { v: 0 }
    top(&!x)
    print_int(x.v)
    println(" chain3")
}
